As you watch this, see what works and

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.010
what you could do differently
to make this stronger.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:43.250
&gt;&gt; [INAUDIBLE]
When I'm not fighting poverty,

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:47.020
I am fighting fires as the assistant
captain of a volunteer fire company.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.760
Now, in our town where the volunteers
supplement a highly skilled career staff,

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:54.770
you have to get to the fire scene
pretty early to get in on any action.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.530
I remember my first fire.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.520
I was the second volunteer on the scene.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:02.559
So there was a pretty good chance
that I was going to get in.

00:15:02.559 --> 00:15:05.427
But still, it was a real foot-raise
against the other volunteers to get to

00:15:05.427 --> 00:15:07.900
the captain in charge to find out
what are assignments would be.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:13.500
When I found the captain he was
having a very engaging conversation

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:18.660
with the homeowner, who was surely having
one of the worst days of her life.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.790
Here it was, the middle of the night.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:25.287
She was standing outside in
the pouring rain under an umbrella,

00:15:25.287 --> 00:15:29.463
in her pajamas, barefoot,
while her house was in flames.

00:15:29.463 --> 00:15:36.342
The other volunteer who had arrived just
before me, let's call him Lex Luther.

00:15:36.342 --> 00:15:39.500
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Got to the captain first and

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:44.327
was asked to go inside and
save the homeowners dog.

00:15:44.327 --> 00:15:48.190
The dog, I was stunned with jealousy.

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:52.169
Here was some lawyer or money manager
who for the rest of his life gets to

00:15:52.169 --> 00:15:56.432
tell people that he went into a burning
building to save a living creature.

00:15:56.432 --> 00:15:58.215
Just because he beat me by five seconds.

00:15:58.215 --> 00:16:01.330
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Well, I was next.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:03.230
The captain waved me over.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.800
He said, Bezos,
I need you to go into the house.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:10.917
I need you to go upstairs,
past the fire, and

00:16:10.917 --> 00:16:15.777
I need you to get this
woman a pair of shoes.

00:16:15.777 --> 00:16:17.534
[LAUGH] I swear.

00:16:17.534 --> 00:16:20.110
Not exactly what I was hoping for,
but off I went.

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:26.020
Up the stairs, down the hall past the real
firefighters who are pretty much done

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:32.760
putting out the fire at this point, into
the master bedroom to get a pair of shoes.

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:37.455
Now, I know what you're thinking,
but I'm no hero.

00:16:37.455 --> 00:16:42.830
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I carried my payload

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:47.875
back down stairs where I met my nemesis
in the precious dog by the front door.

00:16:47.875 --> 00:16:49.450
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; We took our treasures

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:54.150
outside to the homeowner where not
surprisingly his received much

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.280
more attention than did mine.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.000
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; A few week later the department

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.630
received a letter from
the homeowner thanking us for

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:02.360
the valiant effort displayed
in saving her home.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.070
The act of kindness she
notes above all others,

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.290
someone had even gotten
her a pair of shoes.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:15.260
In both my vocation at Robinhood and my
avocation as a volunteer firefighter I am

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.840
witness to acts of generosity and
kindness on a monumental scale but

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:22.440
I'm also witness to acts of grace and
courage on an individual basis.

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.570
And you know what I've learned?

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:29.380
They all matter.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:33.110
So as I look around this room at people
who either have achieved or on their way

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:39.580
to achieving remarkable levels of success,
I would offer this reminder, don't wait.

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.750
Don't wait until you make your
first million to make a difference

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:44.800
in someones life.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:47.240
If you have something to give,
give it now.

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:52.650
Serve from the soup kitchen,
clean up a neighborhood park, be a mentor.

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:57.910
Not everyday is going to offer us
a chance to save somebody's life.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:00.470
But everyday,
offers us an opportunity to affect one.

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:02.990
So get in the game.

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:04.764
Save the shoes.

00:18:04.764 --> 00:18:05.952
Thank you.

00:18:05.952 --> 00:18:09.896
