00:26:57.250 --> 00:27:02.083
These are what I'm going to call the seven

00:27:02.083 --> 00:27:06.096
habits of concise storytellers.

00:27:13.643 --> 00:27:17.200
The first one parachute in.

00:27:19.430 --> 00:27:23.050
There's a great book which
I will mention later.

00:27:23.050 --> 00:27:26.401
Actually, I'm going to share-

00:27:31.927 --> 00:27:35.880
Feel free to glance at this as I speak,
called Leadership Presence.

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:40.510
We brought the folks in from
the aerial group who created this.

00:27:40.510 --> 00:27:45.910
It's great strategies around how
do I as a leader present myself?

00:27:45.910 --> 00:27:49.790
How do I create a stage
presence as a leader?

00:27:49.790 --> 00:27:54.100
And one of the things that they talk about
in there is start the story in the middle.

00:27:55.370 --> 00:27:58.690
Many times, we feel like we've
got to do a lot of prefacing.

00:27:58.690 --> 00:28:02.830
I've gotta give you all this background,
I've gotta give you all this information.

00:28:02.830 --> 00:28:06.740
And really if we can figure out
a way to start in the middle and

00:28:06.740 --> 00:28:09.930
then let people catch up to us, okay?

00:28:09.930 --> 00:28:13.616
So to parachute in with very
little prefacing when Amanda and

00:28:13.616 --> 00:28:18.530
I were planning this session and we were
deciding how we wanted to begin, I said,

00:28:18.530 --> 00:28:22.650
you know what, Amanda,
I'd rather you do the introductions, and

00:28:22.650 --> 00:28:24.700
you do that whole conversation.

00:28:24.700 --> 00:28:27.766
So that I can actually start with a story,
and

00:28:27.766 --> 00:28:31.894
I can start right in with the story,
without any prefacing.

00:28:31.894 --> 00:28:34.714
I think even with the story I told
about Caroline, Catha, and Monica,

00:28:34.714 --> 00:28:38.020
I could have started more in the middle,
but I wanted to have a linear progression.

00:28:39.270 --> 00:28:43.052
So think about your story for
the 20th, how do I parachute in.

00:28:43.052 --> 00:28:45.665
How do I not give too much background.

00:28:45.665 --> 00:28:47.295
Four minutes goes fast.

00:28:47.295 --> 00:28:49.959
If you spend a minute and a half or
two minutes in background,

00:28:49.959 --> 00:28:51.430
you've lost that opportunity.

00:28:53.400 --> 00:29:01.902
Second is select your
first words carefully.

00:29:01.902 --> 00:29:04.983
I would also add final words.

00:29:04.983 --> 00:29:08.399
What were his final words?

00:29:08.399 --> 00:29:08.980
&gt;&gt; Save the shoes.

00:29:08.980 --> 00:29:10.690
&gt;&gt; Save the shoes.

